From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] Migrate 0196-timed-ab-skip.patch

Source: 0196-timed-ab-skip.patch
Core patch, for tools/eglantine-patches as 0196. Ours, a diagnostic.

EDEN_NX2_AB_SKIP=<seconds>;<phase>;<phase>... skips the draws and dispatches of each
phase's programs in turn, so one stand-still minute tests several causes. It works
from the running pipeline's hash, so it also reaches programs from the disk cache,
which EDEN_NX2_REJECT_HASH cannot. The word d16 makes depth clears of a 1600x1600
target clear to 0; a clear that was 0 already does not count as changed, and the log
gives the depth the game asked for. Every phase change logs what was really skipped
and the console's unix time. That clock ran about 48 s ahead of the OBS file names on
5 November, nearly a whole 60 s round, so measure the offset before matching frames.
EDEN_NX2_AB_LOG=1 names every program once with its targets. EDEN_NX2_BORDER_LOG=1
names border colours that get rounded: the console runs without custom ones.

The "Draw skipped" line also gains the target count and the depth target. That is
the one change with no switch, and it only adds text to a log line. run-report.py
reads that line, but only its unchanged start. Nothing else changes unless a variable
is set.

